:: Mom Gym Dinner Report [event mom_quest] {"position":"4650,1075","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "Was That Right?" (mom_gymDinner), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 5.7, part 1 of 2. Optional: only if I sent her to the gym
   dinner ($mom.flags.gymDinner). She comes home from the steakhouse, and the evening itself is her POV passage
   (Mom Gym Dinner POV, the steakhouse background): what happened depends on what I told her before she left
   ($mom.flags.gymDinnerLetHim), his hand on her knee or a light evening and a disappointed client. Its <<EndPov>> goes on
   to part 2 (Mom Gym Dinner Report 2, $povReturn), where she asks: was that right? She wants a yes. My answer there sets
   her feelings toward me and toward $gymOwner.name, and part 2 holds every effect and the NextQuest.
   The first time somebody else touched her because I sent her, and I feel something about it that isn't guilt. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[2].img>><</silent>>
I hear her car at a quarter to eleven, and then nothing for a long time. When I look out the window she's still sitting in the driveway with the engine off and the dome light on, looking at her hands on the steering wheel.

She comes in eventually. She doesn't go upstairs. She comes and stands in the doorway of the living room in the navy dress, holding her heels in one hand and her purse in the other, and her lipstick is gone, worn off by dinner and wine or by something else.

<<Media "images/characters/mom/events/gym_dinner_report/doorway.jpg" 600>>
/* Mom in the living room doorway in the navy dress, barefoot, heels in one hand, the house dark behind her */

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "He signed, right there at the table on the back of the wine list, and then again on the real one when his assistant sent it over. Full price, honey, not a cent off." },
{ who: $player, text: "That's great. Come sit down and tell me how it went." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She sits on the arm of the couch, which she has told me not to do my entire life, and drops her heels on the rug. She takes a breath to start and lets it out again, and then she starts anyway, at the very beginning, with the parking garage.

